## What I had to do beyond the letter of the spec

- **Edited the existing `.context/check-nav-coverage.mjs`** (a ~3-line change). The committed script required a `<repo-root>` argument and exited 2 without it, but the specified wiring `node .context/check-nav-coverage.mjs` passes no argument. I made the root default to the script's own location so `check:nav` actually runs. This means the diff includes that one pre-existing file in addition to the "new files only" list.

## Notes / limitations

- **Pricing page copy is thin in the snapshot.** `/pricing/page.tsx` is a wrapper; the real pricing figures live in the sibling `app/pricing/PricingClient.tsx`, which is not a `page.tsx`, so the extractor (scoped to `app/**/page.tsx` per spec) only captures the page-level wrapper copy. Problem/location pages are fine because their copy is passed as props (string literals) in the page file.
- `public/infographics/*.tsx` contain `┬ú` figures but are outside the audit's `app/**` + `components/**` scope, so they are not flagged.
